It is the year 80pc, and you are in the town of Belcaer, waiting to meet with Abeth Harbrook. The local officer of the Chandlers Guild, she has promised a reward for anyone who can bring her a local bandit - alive or dead.
-> exposition

=== exposition
"King Bark," as the bandit calls himself, has been mugging travelers for months. Recently, his attacks have gotten more bold. He's begun to steal livestock from local farms, and it's rumored he's responsible for the arson of a local dairy.
You've been waiting for around twenty minutes, when Ms. Harbook comes out of her office to greet you. You stand up to introduce yourself.
-> introChoices

=== introChoices
+ "Ms. Harbrook. I'm Jasmine Honeypot. The Chandlers Guild sent me to see how your investigation into 'King Bark' has been going." -> honeypotIntro
+ "Missus Harbrook? I'm Alfrin Gerr. I think it's this King that stole my workhorse. I'd love a chance to get at him." -> gerrIntro
+ "Hello. My name is Puro Blan, Professor of Thaumobiology at Astar University. I'd like to hear about this 'bandit' of yours." -> blanIntro

=== honeypotIntro ===
Ms. Harbrook flushes as pink as her floral-print vest.

"Oh, you are? Well, I suppose you can guess: if you're here, it's not going well," she says, walking back into her office.

"We've always had to tolerate highway robbery - the marshes everywhere make sure everyone sticks to the main trade road, and well, it's not like the thieves could get honest work if they wanted it: nothing grows in the Gloaming.

"But what we - the Chandlers Guild - won't tolerate is attacks on the citizens of Belcaer. This town is our southern-most outpost, and we need to let the locals know that our assets aren't up for grabs, the way all these independent traders' are."

You frown. You're quite aware of the strategic importance of Belcaer: that's why your bosses sent you to this backwater. You don't need this clunky exposition, but the cadence of the Belcaeran accent hasn't let you interrupt.

"And we've had problems with overly-aggressive bandits before, but they were always just locals who got a little too hungry, and hiring them out always worked. We'd love to try and bribe this latest threat, but 'King Bark,' as he calls himself, has been hard to find.

"And honestly, I'm not sure if he'd take the money, even if we could find him. Some of Bark's behavior I can understand, like sticking up passing traders. But why burn a grain silo? Something about this is different, I tell you."

It takes you a moment before you realize Harbrook is finished speaking. That's it? That's her information?

+ "So... you can't find him?" -> honeypotIntro2

=== honeypotIntro2

"Oh! Well. No. But I think I know where he is. Process of deduction," Abeth Harbrook says proudly, while pulling out a map of the Gloaming.

-> gloamingMap
-> honeypotIntro3

=== honeypotIntro3

ARgble Barlrlr

-> ending

=== gloamingMap
You see Belcaer, situated on a mesa raised by powerful magic-users many centuries ago. There's the single trade road through the Gloaming, created by those same wizards.

There are a few other markings on the map, smaller roads and keys indicating smaller villages and the occasional ruin from a long-dead empire.

Abeth put her finger over the marker for one such ruin.

